            "is_private": false,
            "tags": [],
            "bug_id": 19032,
            "text": "Created attachment 3646\nPatch.\n\nGETVAR has a fallback to GET_BINDING_CELL_CACHE when the smallcache slot is R_NilValue (eval.c line 5896), but SETVAR lacks the equivalent. This means SETVAR relies on a prior GETVAR to prime the cache. When no GETVAR has done so, every SETVAR falls through to defineVar.\n\nThe patch adds the same R_NilValue fallback to SETVAR's smallcache path, and a SET_CACHED_BINDING call after the defineVar fallback to prime the cache on first binding creation.\n\nThis gives a small but meaningful optimization for loop bodies of the form:\n\n```\nfor (i in 1:n) {\n\n  # assign variables (SETVAR before GETVAR)\n  x <- 1\n  y <- 2\n\n  # use variables (GETVAR)\n  z <- x + y\n\n}\n```",
            "count": 0,
            "creation_time": "2026-03-27T07:14:13Z"
          },
